EF AI Workspace (#224): chat page redesign, owner-approved 2026-10-25 («اعتمد التصميم ونفذه بكل دقة واحترافية»), with
web search always on and skills that work with it. Compared with ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude and Copilot (the approved design
artifact holds the comparison and all 21 states, phone and desktop).

- Skills as text (utils/efaiwSkills.ts, Chat/Input/SkillsCommand.tsx, hooks/Chat/useChatFunctions.ts): Qwen stops its
  built-in search whenever a request carries tools (#213), and LibreChat's skills switch adds its skill tools. A skill
  picked with «$» or from «+» is now fetched and attached as a plain-text context file `<title>.efaiw-skill.txt` (the
  route a long paste takes); a chat never turns the skill tools on (`ephemeralAgent.skills` is false at submit). The
  «$» list opens with «How to use a skill» in three steps, shows each skill's description as its example, the
  auto-applied brand skill first with «Automatic» and its readable name, and ends with «Manage skills» and «Create a
  skill». The upload runs in the always-mounted wrapper, so its slow-upload notice is cleared when it ends.
- Composer: «+» (Chat/Input/ToolsDropdown.tsx) is a file from the device or from Documents, a ready command («/») and a
  skill («$»), memory, then a line saying web search runs by itself; the internet and skills switches are gone. A chat
  saved on a no-search twin shows «No internet ×», which moves it back (InternetBadge.tsx); a model change always picks
  the spec with search (composerModes.ts). Placeholders by state (hooks/Input/useTextarea.ts): default with «/» and
  «$», a picked skill, attached files, a temporary chat. A picked skill is a green «$» chip on the box and the sent
  message, a long paste reads «Pasted text» (Files/FileContainer.tsx); skill attachments are not listed on Documents
  (EfPages/EfFilesPage.tsx). A one-time skills tip above a new chat's box (EfSkillsTip.tsx). Pro's line «Doesn't search
  the web for now» in the model menu (SpeedSelector.tsx). On phones the temporary chat is in the new chat's header
  (Chat/Header.tsx).
- Replies: the model's name moves from above the reply (kept for screen readers, brand.css) to the end of its toolbar;
  the toolbar is copy, download, regenerate, rating and «More» (Chat/Messages/HoverButtons.tsx, EfReplyMore.tsx: share
  the chat first, read aloud, edit, fork to a new chat, retry with another Baseer model). Touch screens show an older
  reply's actions on tap (ui/MessageRow.tsx). The download menu names the file and lists each format as a badge with
  what it is for (DownloadReply.tsx, useDocumentDownloads.tsx); both menus portal into <main> (its landmark and
  direction). A letter or minutes gets a Word/PDF bar (EfReplyExtras.tsx `EfDocBar`).
- Suggestions under the latest finished reply (utils/efaiwFollowUps.ts, EfReplyExtras.tsx `EfFollowUps`): Baseer ends
  a reply with a fenced `efaiw-followups` block (librechat.yaml): two or three questions from the reply and up to two
  actions from a fixed list; questions send as they read, actions send a short request in the reply's language.
  Without a valid block the actions come from rules on the reply's shape. The block is never shown, copied,
  downloaded, read aloud or kept in an artifact (Content/Markdown.tsx, useCopyToClipboard.ts, DownloadReply.tsx).
- Strings (en/translation.json; ar.json). Tests: efaiwFollowUps.spec, efaiwSkills.spec, EfReplyExtras.spec,
  SkillsCommand.spec (the text route), FileContainer.spec (chips), HoverButtons.spec (editing in «More»),
  useTextarea.spec (agent config mocks).

